; colsum_overflow: a column whose partial sum leaves the i64 range must
; raise.
;
; The negative mirror of rowsum_overflow: linear = [i64::MIN, -1, 1] down
; a 3x1 grid. The partial sum after the second row is -2^63 - 1, which is
; not representable, so COLSUM raises ArithmeticOverflow.
;
; Discriminating for the same reason: a wrapping implementation walks
; i64::MIN -> i64::MAX -> i64::MIN and pushes the exactly correct total,
; and a descending fold of the same column never leaves the range.

PUSH 3
BQMX r0

PUSH 3           ; rows
PUSH 1           ; cols
RESIZE r0

PUSH 0
PUSH -9223372036854775808
SETLINE r0
PUSH 1
PUSH -1
SETLINE r0
PUSH 2
PUSH 1
SETLINE r0

PUSH 0           ; col
COLSUM r0
HALT
